---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import CtaBand from "../components/CtaBand.astro";
import { processSteps } from "../data/site";
---

<Base
  title="How a Project Works | Andre Preer, Springfield IL"
  description="How a landscape or stone project with Andre Preer proceeds: contact, a site visit, a proposal, the build, and a final walkthrough. No promised start date."
>
  <main id="main">
    <section>
      <div class="wrap prose">
        <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ name: "Home", href: "/" }, { name: "Process", href: "/process/" }]} />
        <p class="eyebrow">Process</p>
        <h1>From the first call to the walkthrough</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          The sequence is ordinary on purpose. Timing depends on the property, the season, and the scope you agree to. Nothing on this page is a promise of a start date or a price.
        </p>
        <ol class="process-list">
          {
            processSteps.map((step) => (
              <li>
                <span class="step-n">{step.n}</span>
                <h2>{step.title}</h2>
                <p>{step.text}</p>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
        <p>If you want the shorter version of how the design itself is approached — walking the site, then drawing the whole picture — that is also described on the <a href="/about/">about page</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <CtaBand heading="The first step is a conversation." text="Call, or send the town and a description of the property. You are not committing to a build by asking." />
  </main>
</Base>
